schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Sarafu Network supports 26,000+ people across ~290 Kenyan communities
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    Sarafu Network, run by the Kenyan nonprofit Grassroots Economics,
    supports 26,000+ people across roughly 290 communities using commitment
    pools (shared accounts where members issue Community Asset Vouchers) and
    runs on the Celo blockchain via USSD, so it works on basic phones without
    internet.
  evidence: >-
    Stated in is-community-ready.md's "The One Failure Mode to Plan Around"
    section, linking to Grassroots Economics: Sarafu Network.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/is-community-ready.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used as the counter-example to founder-dependent local currencies —
    Sarafu survives because it grew from existing community trust networks
    and no single person is load-bearing.
  uncertainty: >-
    Figures (26,000+ people, ~290 communities) are as stated in the article;
    not independently re-verified against Grassroots Economics' current
    reporting for this ingestion.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/is-community-ready.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
